blurb = "Depicts farmers harvesting burdock roots in Iyo Province (modern-day Ehime prefecture). The text in the top right corner explains that although burdock is grown throughout Japan, it is a specialty of Iyo. It claims that the largest roots reach over 1.2 meters in length, and 9 to 12 centimeters in diameter, but remain tender and flavorful despite the size."
